# Architecture

- Content-driven: page copy and IA live in `src/content/**` and `src/config/**`; UI consumes typed data.
- Keep layers separate: `config` → `content`/`lib` → `components` → `app` routes.
- Prefer composition over inheritance; one concern per module.
- Do not invent dollar prices — use `Custom` / sales CTAs from `src/config/pricing.ts`.
- No page UI scaffolding unless asked; extend existing patterns.
- Shared types belong in `src/types`; avoid duplicating interfaces in content files.
- Integrations/CRM/analytics are pluggable stubs in `src/lib/**` — register providers, do not hardcode vendors in UI.
